---
import Button from "../components/Button.astro";
import Container from "../components/Container.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import WorkflowStep from "../components/WorkflowStep.astro";
import WorkflowShowcase from "../components/WorkflowShowcase.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="How Syntila works — Shared Spaces for people and AI"
  description="See how Syntila connects people, shared Spaces and Threads, and AI Workers that run on a member's own computer."
>
  <Section>
    <Container>
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="How it works"
        title="From shared ideas to verified results."
        description="Create a Space for yourself or a group, and use Threads to keep each topic together. Your AI tools run on a connected computer."
        headingLevel={1}
      />

      <div class="section-block-gap">
        <ul class="workflow-steps" role="list">
          <WorkflowStep visual="space" title="Create a Space and open a Thread">
            <p>Create a Space for your project or your group, then start a Thread for each topic to keep its conversation and history together.</p>
          </WorkflowStep>
          <WorkflowStep visual="invite" title="Invite others when you want">
            <p>Work on your own, or share an invite by email or link. Others can join on the web or mobile without their own AI account.</p>
          </WorkflowStep>
          <WorkflowStep visual="connect" title="Connect & share AI">
            <p>One member connects a computer with Syntila Workspace and chooses which AI Workers to share. See <a href="#host-needs">what the host needs</a>.</p>
          </WorkflowStep>
          <WorkflowStep visual="collaborate" title="Collaborate and choose a Workflow">
            <p>Ask a Worker with the Thread as context, or discuss the task with others. Choose Chat, Work, Research, or Implement to match the task.</p>
          </WorkflowStep>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="section-block-gap-lg" id="host-needs">
        <SectionHeader
          eyebrow="For the host"
          title="What the person who connects a computer needs."
          description="Install Workspace on the computer that powers the AI. Access your Spaces from the web or mobile, including when you are away from that computer."
        />
        <div class="host-requirements">
          <article class="host-requirement">
            <div class="host-requirement__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><rect x="7" y="10" width="34" height="28" rx="5"/><path d="m14 19 5 5-5 5m9 0h10"/></svg></div>
            <div><h3>An AI tool, signed in</h3><p>Install and sign in to the AI command-line tools you want to share, such as Codex CLI, Claude Code, or Antigravity CLI.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="host-requirement">
            <div class="host-requirement__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><rect x="6" y="9" width="36" height="25" rx="4"/><path d="M18 40h12m-6-6v6m-7-19h14m-7-7v14"/></svg></div>
            <div><h3>Syntila Workspace</h3><p>Connect your computer to Syntila and make its AI tools available to your Space. <a href="/downloads/">Download Workspace</a>.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="host-requirement">
            <div class="host-requirement__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><path d="M24 7v17m-8-13a16 16 0 1 0 16 0"/><circle cx="36" cy="35" r="5" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"/></svg></div>
            <div><h3>A computer that stays on</h3><p>Keep it awake and online for its Workers to answer. When it is off, people can still read and write messages.</p></div>
          </article>
          <article class="host-requirement">
            <div class="host-requirement__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><path d="M24 6 38 12v10c0 9-5 15-14 20-9-5-14-11-14-20V12L24 6Z"/><path d="m17 24 5 5 9-10"/></svg></div>
            <div><h3>A plan that allows sharing</h3><p>Before others use a Worker you connected, <a href="/faq/#sharing-subscriptions">check your AI provider’s sharing rules</a>.</p></div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="section-block-gap-lg" id="workflows">
        <SectionHeader
          eyebrow="Workflows"
          title="Four ways to ask."
        />
        <WorkflowShowcase illustrated />
      </div>

      <div class="section-block-gap-lg">
        <SectionHeader
          eyebrow="Architecture"
          title="Four layers from conversation to local execution."
        />
        <div class="execution-path-strip architecture-flow" role="region" aria-label="Syntila architecture flow">
          <div class="execution-path-step"><div class="architecture-flow__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><rect x="6" y="8" width="36" height="29" rx="4"/><path d="M6 16h36M13 12h.1M18 12h.1M13 23h12m-12 6h19"/></svg></div>
            <span>Syntila app</span>
            <strong>Spaces &amp; Threads</strong>
            <p>People join Spaces, talk in Threads, and send requests to Workers at <code>app.syntila.app</code>.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="execution-path-step"><div class="architecture-flow__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><path d="M15 34H11a8 8 0 0 1-1-16 14 14 0 0 1 27 2 7 7 0 0 1 0 14h-4"/><rect x="17" y="26" width="14" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M20 26v-3a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"/></svg></div>
            <span>Syntila Cloud</span>
            <strong>History &amp; permissions</strong>
            <p>Stores Thread history, checks each member's role and the Space's permissions, and passes requests to the right computer.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="execution-path-step"><div class="architecture-flow__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><rect x="6" y="9" width="36" height="26" rx="3"/><path d="M18 40h12m-6-5v5M13 18h22m-22 7h14"/></svg></div>
            <span>Syntila Workspace</span>
            <strong>The host computer</strong>
            <p>A background service on the member's computer receives the request and starts the right AI tool.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="execution-path-step"><div class="architecture-flow__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 48 48" fill="none"><rect x="7" y="9" width="34" height="30" rx="4"/><path d="m15 19 5 5-5 5m10 0h9"/></svg></div>
            <span>AI tools</span>
            <strong>Provider CLIs &amp; MCP</strong>
            <p>Codex CLI, Claude Code, Antigravity CLI, or a custom MCP Worker does the work, signed in with the host's own account.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="actions actions--center section-block-gap-lg">
        <Button href="https://app.syntila.app" label="Open Syntila" event="cta.open_app" />
        <Button href="/workers/" label="Explore AI & Workers" variant="secondary" />
      </div>
    </Container>
  </Section>
</SiteLayout>
